Specifications only (no code, comment or table copied): mainline Linux drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8750.c and tcsrcc-sm8750.c,
include/dt-bindings/clock/qcom,sm8750-gcc.h, drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c and pcie-designware.h,
drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-pcie.c and phy-qcom-qmp-pcs-v7.h, drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8750.c (register offsets, bit
positions, the DesignWare LTSSM L0 value); Project-SunUEFI (unixnu-research/Project-SunUEFI) patches/linux/7.3/0001-platform.patch,
a GPL-2.0 kernel patch read for facts only (the WCN7861 supply voltage ranges in WifiHw.h's comment); the piano boot DT
(out/inputs/piano-boot.dtb), which is where every rail, voltage range, pin, window and stream of levels 2 to 4 comes from; ARM IHI
0062 (SMMUv2: SMR, S2CR, IDR0/IDR1); the MHI specification's register and state names as mainline drivers/bus/mhi and the vendor
MHI host use them (behaviour only, no code, comment or table). Not read and not used for anything: any Qualcomm binary (no reverse
engineering of vendor firmware or drivers). The firmware itself is never part of this repository: level 4 reads
image/peach/amss20.bin out of the tablet's own modem_a partition at run time (LicenseRef-Proprietary-Firmware, no
redistribution).
